			"notes": "Complete rewrite. One dependency-free jar now covers every Bukkit-family server from Minecraft **1.8.8 to 26.2** (Spigot, Paper, Purpur, Folia), plus builds for Velocity, BungeeCord, Fabric and NeoForge.\n\nThe Bukkit jar went from 771 KB to about 30 KB: the shaded HTTP stack was replaced with the client built into Java, so there are no third-party classes left to clash with other plugins.\n\n### Which file\n- **`DiscordChatLogger-Bukkit-2.0.0.jar`** — Spigot / Paper / Purpur / Folia, any version 1.8.8+\n- `DiscordChatLogger-Velocity-2.0.0.jar` — Velocity 3.x and 4.x\n- `DiscordChatLogger-Bungee-2.0.0.jar` — BungeeCord / Waterfall\n- `DiscordChatLogger-Fabric-<mc>-2.0.0.jar` / `-NeoForge-<mc>-2.0.0.jar` — pick your Minecraft version\n\n### Fixed\n- Ran only on 1.20–1.20.6; now 1.8.8 through 26.2 from a single file\n- Used only the chat event Paper has deprecated for removal; Paper's modern event is now used where present\n- One HTTP request per message, which Discord rate-limits on a busy server; messages are now batched, and rate limits pause and retry instead of dropping\n- Players could ping `@everyone` or any role by typing it; no message can trigger a mention now\n- Players could reshape the Discord log with markdown; chat text is now escaped\n- Messages cancelled by other plugins (muted players, filters) were still relayed\n- Commands are never relayed on proxies, so a mistyped `/login` cannot leak\n- `plugin.yml` described this as \"the best currency plugin out there\"\n\n### New\n- Player name and skin as the Discord message author\n- `/discordchatlogger` with `reload`, `test` and `status`\n- Optional join/leave and death relaying, and a `server-name` label for sharing one channel\n\n### Not supported\nFabric on Minecraft 26.x — Minecraft 26 ships unobfuscated, so Mojang publishes no mappings and Fabric Loom still requires them. Use the NeoForge build there.\n\nEvery published build was verified by booting a real server and confirming the message reached a webhook. See the README for the full matrix."
		}
